This section studies KL-regularized reinforcement learning fine-tuning of audio-video two-tower diffusion models under the protocol of “alternately fixing a single-modality complete denoising trajectory”.
We introduce a common reference joint law P 0 P_{0} , and specify the two single-tower operation kernels as the regular conditional kernels of P 0 P_{0} ;
the reward r r is bounded measurable, and β > 0 \beta>0 . We define the exponentially tilted joint law d ​ P ∗ / d ​ P 0 ∝ e r / β \,\mathrm{d}P^{*}/\,\mathrm{d}P_{0}\propto e^{r/\beta} , and construct the two conditional Gibbs optimal kernels K v ∗ , K a ∗ K_{v}^{*},K_{a}^{*} .
Under the Dobrushin contraction condition δ v ​ δ a < 1 \delta_{v}\delta_{a}<1 , we prove: P ∗ P^{*} is the unique global optimum of the joint KL-regularized objective; K v ∗ , K a ∗ K_{v}^{*},K_{a}^{*} are the unique optimal kernels of the conditional subproblems, respectively, and are automatically compatible;
the systematic-scan Gibbs chain with kernels K v ∗ , K a ∗ K_{v}^{*},K_{a}^{*} has a unique stationary distribution P ∗ P^{*} ;
starting from any initial joint law, the joint laws of both sampling phases converge geometrically in total variation to P ∗ P^{*} , with an explicit convergence rate.
If the model implements K v ∗ , K a ∗ K_{v}^{*},K_{a}^{*} via a non-interfering exact kernel oracle, then both the training rollouts and the inference distribution using the same alternating full-trajectory protocol possess the above convergence properties.

